Cell["\<\
After acquiring the proper variables for  our model we look at the data that \
we have. This is not interpolated data, it is not smoothed. Interpolation is \
what will allow us to have better higher order derivatives, for now what I am \
plotting below is the model without interpolation and just the data extracted \
as is. 

Our next move is to define the end of inflation using a mask, we can do this \
either value based or index based. I would like to plot this on top of our \
grid plot above to make sure that it is taking up the correct area.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.964179977421969*^9, 3.964180002964447*^9}, {
  3.9641800396564493`*^9, 3.9641800404769*^9}, {3.964180951981312*^9, 
  3.964180955867197*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d6f7c4e3-a4a4-4223-998b-\
46d18c1ca500"],

